Q: How to move text of a banner image while sliding? A: <p>The basic idea is to use CSS transitions to make it look like there's an infinite amount of text, no JS needed. In the example below I've created an animation that will move the text out of bounds at the top and on the right, and straight after it will teleport the text to the bottom and to the left respectively.</p>
<p>You can make this animation as fancy or as simple as you'd like. For example, I added an opacity transition to the arrow as well to make it appear a bit less harshly. If you remove this opacity you can see how the text kinda teleports.</p>
<pre><code>

<div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>/* placeholder slide */
.slide {
  aspect-ratio: 16/9;
  background: #773c32;
  height: 500px;
  justify-content: center;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  padding: 20px;
}

/* some basic style to replicate https://kasian.com/ */
.btn {
  border: 1px solid white;
  display: flex;
  gap: 80px;
  color: white;
  padding: 20px;
  width: 100%;
  max-width: fit-content;
  height: 20px;
  text-decoration: none;
  position: relative;
}

.btn-arrow, .btn-text {
  position: relative; /* needed to manipulate the animations */
}

.btn:hover {
  overflow: hidden; /* this will clip off any bit of the animated text when it's outside the parent */
}

/* apply the hover animations */
.btn:hover .btn-arrow {
  animation: whoosh-right .75s ease-in-out;
}

.btn:hover .btn-text {
  animation: whoosh-top .75s ease-in-out;
}

/* animate the arrow to move right, makes it go slightly translucent before it fades back in from the left */
@keyframes whoosh-right {
  0%, 100% {
    left: 0%;
    opacity: 1;
  }

  50% {
    left: 30px;
    opacity: 0;
  }

  50.1% {
    left: -30px;
    opacity: 0;
  }
}

/* Move the text outside the button's  borders, once outside, instantly teleports to the bottom and moves up again, giving the feel that there's an infinite amount of text */
@keyframes whoosh-top {
  0%, 100% {
    top: 0%;
  }

  50% {
    top: -50px;
  }

  50.1% {
    top: 50px;
  }
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div class="slide"&gt;
  &lt;h2&gt;Hello I am your slide title&lt;/h2&gt;
  &lt;a href="#" class="btn"&gt;
    &lt;span class="btn-text"&gt;Find out more&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="btn-arrow"&gt;-&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
